#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:17
msgid "16. Bluetooth Motion Monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:19
msgid "This last project is the only one that talks **both ways at the same time**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:21
msgid "The board streams the tilt of an **MPU6050** to the phone - a notification on **C305**, twice per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:23
msgid "The phone can **stop and restart** that stream by writing ``P`` or ``S`` to **C304**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:25
msgid "Every other chapter used one direction only. Here you watch both, and you can see the difference between the two characteristics clearly: one carries data **to** you, the other carries your command **back**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:31
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:35
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:41
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:42
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`cpn_mpu6050`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:47
msgid "2. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:49
msgid "Open the ``16-Bluetooth_motion_monitor.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\16-Bluetooth_motion_monitor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:53
msgid "Install **Adafruit MPU6050** and **Adafruit Unified Sensor** from the Library Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:55
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:57
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:69
msgid "If you read ``[!] no MPU6050 found``, the sensor is not answering on A4/A5 - check SDA, SCL, VCC and GND before going any further."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:74
msgid "**Leave the board flat and still while it powers up.** The sketch takes ten readings in the first second and stores that position as the zero point, so a board lying on the table shows ``X:0.0 Y:0.0`` instead of the few degrees that every sensor has of its own. The two numbers printed on the ``zero:`` line are what it measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:81
msgid "3. Watch and Control at the Same Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:83
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:85
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C305**, then tap **Subscribe**. Lines start to arrive twice per second:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:96
msgid "**The numbers are degrees.** ``0`` means the board lies flat, ``90`` means it stands on its edge, and the sign tells you which way it leans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:103
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:104
msgid "What it is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:105
msgid "``X``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:106
msgid "tilt **around the X axis** - the board leans left or right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:107
msgid "``Y``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:108
msgid "tilt **around the Y axis** - the board leans forward or backward"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:112
msgid "On a real board you will see ``X:-1.0 Y:-3.0`` rather than ``0.0 0.0``. That is not a fault: every MPU6050 is soldered at a very small angle and has a small offset of its own. A few degrees while lying flat is normal, and it does not change what you see when you tilt the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:117
msgid "Close to vertical the two numbers influence each other a little - tilt towards ``Y:80`` and ``X`` starts to move as well. That is how this kind of angle is calculated, not a wiring problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:121
msgid "Now go back to the service list and open **C304**. Write ``P`` - the stream stops at once and the Serial Monitor prints ``Streaming paused``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:129
msgid "This is the interesting part: **the subscription on C305 is still open**, but nothing arrives any more, because the board stopped sending. Data only flows when the sketch decides to send it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:133
msgid "Write ``S`` to start again - the lines come back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:137
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:139
msgid "**Two directions in one loop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:153
msgid "The first block **reads**, the second **writes**. Both run in the same ``loop()`` and neither blocks the other - that is why the stream keeps flowing while the phone can still send a command at any moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:157
msgid "**Tilt instead of raw acceleration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:164
msgid "The sensor reports acceleration in ``m/s^2``, which is hard to read. ``atan2`` turns it into an angle in degrees: ``0`` flat, ``90`` standing on its side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:167
msgid "**The zero point**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:182
msgid "Ten readings are averaged because a single one jumps around by a degree or two. The average is then subtracted from every later reading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:190
msgid "Without this step a board lying flat would show ``X:-1.0 Y:-3.0`` and a student would think something is wrong. With it, ``0.0`` really means flat - and that is also how a real product does it (usually with a button to re-zero whenever you like)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:194
msgid "**Half a second between lines**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:201
msgid "BLE cannot carry an endless stream; a line every 500 ms is smooth on screen and still leaves the module time for the command channel. Sending every loop would flood the buffer and make ``P`` arrive late."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:205
msgid "**Why the pause is a flag and not a stop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/16-iot_Bluetooth_motion_monitor.rst:211
msgid "Nothing in the BLE connection is closed when you send ``P`` - the sketch simply stops writing. The connection, the subscription and the characteristic all stay alive, which is why ``S`` works instantly afterwards."
msgstr ""
